! REPRODUCER: strap_asm.py refuses a blank between a radix specifier and
! its number in an instruction's address field.  Found 2026-11-15
! transcribing C22-6578 Problem 2.9 (problem_2_9.strap), printed p.21
! (PDF 22), whose statement TEST is printed, with the blank,
!
!       TEST    KFI(BU, 2), (2) 10,4        'test if floating-point
!
! THE RULE.  C22-6578 printed p.21, Problem 2.8 comment (d): "Normally
! the STRAP assembler ignores all blanks in instructions and pseudo-
! instructions.  An exception is made for pseudo-instructions
! specifying alphabetic characters".  The same page's other KFI lines
! are printed "(2)0000", "(2)1000, 4", without the blank, and those
! assemble.
!
! strap_asm:  AssemblerError, "cannot parse expression '(2) 10' at
!             '(2) 10'".  OBSERVED 2026-11-15.
! FIXED 2026-11-23: WITHB and NOB assemble to the same word.  The
! grammar's rule is C22-6729 printed p.20 (PDF 20), Chart MAIN Box 5:
! "GETCHA does not give blanks to main flow unless main flow has
! turned on the indicator, Gcaz" (on only for an alphabetic DD and
! the ID field).
!
! tests/check_radix_blank.py is the registered check.
! problem_2_9.strap now writes the statement with the printed blank.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   BEW, $
        CNOP
NOB     KFI(BU, 2), (2)10,4
WITHB   KFI(BU, 2), (2) 10,4
        END, START
